#[doc = r#"This message specifies the Actions allocated to a System.  Allocation can be done manually by operators, by an allocation service or a combination.  This message decouples Action allocation from kinematic, action and other types of planning; Action allocations can be created, updated and approved independent of other *Plans.  It enables any type of *Plan to be a constraint on Action allocation.
An ActionPlan can be an input and/or output of planning processes.  For example the ActionPlan for the top System in a hierarchical System of System could be an input to an Action allocation service that the produces an ActionPlan per subordinate System with their subset of allocated Actions.
Additional details such as timing, dependencies, decomposition, etc. can be added during the Action allocation process and captured in the ActionPlan to supplement the information in the allocated Actions themselves.
An ActionPlan can be created discretely or as part of a MissionPlan that includes other *Plans.  An ActionPlan can only be activated and executed as part of a MissionPlan.  A MissionPlan can be used to plan the execution order of multiple ActionPlans and *Plans in general.  An ActionPlan can be subject to approval per Approval* messages.  Planning, approval, activation and execution state information for an ActionPlan are given in other ActionPlan* messages.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1."#]
