#[doc = r#"This message is a request to cancel CommSupport which has been allocated and planned.  A planning input such as Effect, CommSupport, Task and DMPI can't easily be canceled or removed from the System due to race conditions between their various users and publishers, inevitability of the associated activity, etc.  Additionally, the operator or service initiating the cancellation might be different than the one that manages RequirementSets and/or issues *PlanCommand, introducing additional race conditions.  In order to avoid race conditions, receive positive feedback on the success of the cancellation and allow canceled messages/objects to remain in the system for historical purposes, an explicit CommSupportCancelCommand is necessary.  A CommSupportCancelCommand shall result in the CommSupport being canceled unless execution was already inevitable.  If the CommSupport was inevitable and started executing but can be stopped (such as a long collection CommSupport) it shall cancel as soon as possible.  CommSupportCancelCommand shall result in managers of RequirementSets to remove the associated CommSupport, thereby removing the CommSupport from the next planning cycle.  Services other than those that manage RequirementSets and execute activities aren't required to handle CommSupportCancelCommand.  CommSupportCancelCommand doesn't necessarily trigger a replan (there isn't a corresponding planning trigger), therefore a System could continue to navigate routes related to the canceled CommSupport, even though the CommSupport won't occur.  A subsequent replan could exclude the CommSupport.  Status or feedback for this message is given through CommSupportCancelCommandStatus but the resulting status of the CommSupport is given through CommSupportStatus.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Command-2."#]
