#[doc = r#"This message specifies the communications support ("comm support") associated with a System.  Details of comm support are described in the associated CommSupport message; the CommSupportPlan bundles CommSupport messages into sets associated with a System.  A CommSupportPlan can be developed manually by operators, by a plannin service or a combination.  This message decouples comm support from kinematic, task, action and other types of planning; comm support can be developed, updated and approved independent of other *Plans.  It enables any type of *Plan to be a constraint on comm support and vice-versa.

A CommSupportPlan can be an input and/or output of planning processes.  For example the CommSupportPlan for the top System in a hierarchical System of System could be an input to a comms planning service that then produces a CommSupportPlan per subordinate System with their subset of allocated comms support.

Additional details such as timing, dependencies, decomposition, etc. can be added during the comm support planning process and captured in the CommSupportPlan to supplement the information in the associated CommSupport messages themselves.

A CommSupportPlan can be created discretely or as part of a MissionPlan that includes other *Plans.  A CommSupportPlan can only be activated and executed as part of a MissionPlan.  A MissionPlan can be used to plan the execution order of multiple CommSupportPlans and *Plans in general.  A CommSupportPlan can be subject to approval per Approval* messages.  Planning, approval, activation and execution state information for a CommSupportPlan are given in other CommSupportPlan* messages.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1."#]
