#[doc = r#"This message indicates who has various levels of control of a System, how the System is configured to be controlled, its autonomous/self-control capability, and its planning capability.  UCI Systems are collections of controllable capabilities that can be pseudo-independently shared/controlled by multiple users; this message indicates the current controllers.  UCI Systems support one or more forms of control via UCI messages/interfaces; this message indicates which categories of UCI control messages are accepted.  UCI Systems have various levels of control automation; this message indicates autonomous/self-control capabilities for each control category.  UCI Systems have a variety of planning processes; this message advertises supported processes.  The messages PlanningFunction*, Approval*, MissionContingencyAlert and ControlStatus are closely related.  They use a common taxonomy of autonomous functions (task allocation, route planning, mission activation and mission execution), triggers for those functions (new threats, new zones, failures, etc.) and results of those functions (dropped Tasks, changes in vulnerability, etc.).  ControlStatus indicates the full set of available autonomous functions/settings of a System.  PlanningFunction* indicates how the available settings are currently configured.  MissionContingencyAlert indicates an autonomous function/setting that has been triggered.  Approval* messages allow Operators to approve the results of autonomous responses as needed.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Status-1."#]
