#[doc = r#"This message contains information identifying an Entity that was not observed in the time frame and location expected.  In Space operations, a Resident Space Object (RSO) entity is considered "lost" if it does not have any associated metric observations within the last 30 days. Other Entity-related messages characterize an Entity at a point in time based on an observation or propagation/prediction.  In contrast, this message indicates  a previously established Entity wasn't observed as expected/planned along with metrics characterizing the loss. For example, if several sensors are tracking an Entity and one sensor "loses" the Entity, this message would provide those details. This message could be provided directly by an observing System that produces other Entity* messages, by a Service that analyzes Entity* messages from other Systems over time, etc. This message applies to any object that is being observed by a sensor suite (including blue, red, and gray objects). This message also provides the details of an event occurring after enough data has been gathered to create this message.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Status-1."#]
