#[doc = r#"This message is the list of current, active Requirements from a Requirement source.  It provides a mechanism for Requirement creators to freely create and publish Tasks without them being included in a planning cycle initiated elsewhere.  When a Requirement creator has created a coherent set of Requirements that is ready for consideration for planning, the Requirements are summarized in this message and published as an indication to the operator or service that initiates planning to include them in the next planning cycle.  The ManagingSystemID element allows a Requirement creator to assign responsibility to its own System or other Systems.  For example, a System could assign planning responsibility for a set of Requirements to a sibling or subordinate System.  When a planning cycle occurs and a Requirement can't be allocated this message/object maintains the current, active To-Do list regardless of planning results from each Requirement source's perspective without relying on MissionPlan, MissionPlanCommand and Requirement states.  Each source of this message is expected to monitor for RequirementCancel requests and removed Requirements accordingly; canceled Requirements should be removed from the RequirementSet list in order to exclude them from the next planning cycle.UCI_PRIMITIVE: DataRecord-1."#]
