#[doc = r#"This message is a request to cancel a Response which has been allocated and planned.  A planning input such as Effect, Response, Task and DMPI can't easily be canceled or removed from the System due to race conditions between their various users and publishers, inevitability of the associated activity, etc.  Additionally, the operator or service initiating the cancellation might be different than the one that manages RequirementSets and/or issues *PlanCommand, introducing additional race conditions.  In order to avoid race conditions, receive positive feedback on the success of the cancellation and allow canceled messages/objects to remain in the system for historical purposes, an explicit ResponseCancelCommand is necessary.  A ResponseCancelCommand shall result in the Response being canceled unless execution was already inevitable.  If the Response was inevitable and started executing but can be stopped (such as a long collection Response) it shall cancel as soon as possible.  ResponseCancelCommand shall result in managers of RequirementSets to remove the associated Response, thereby removing the Response from the next planning cycle.  Services other than those that manage RequirementSets and execute activities aren't required to handle ResponseCancelCommand.  ResponseCancelCommand doesn't necessarily trigger a replan (there isn't a corresponding planning trigger), therefore a System could continue to navigate routes related to the canceled Response, even though the Response won't occur.  A subsequent replan could exclude the Response.  Status or feedback for this message is given through ResponseCancelCommandStatus but the resulting status of the Response is given through ResponseStatus.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Command-2."#]
