#[doc = r#"This message specifies planned activities for a System with a RoutePlan.  A "Route Activity" is any *Capability-related activity planned in context of the kinematic RoutePlan of the System.  Activities are the planned implementation details of Effects, Actions, Tasks, Capability Commands, etc.  Route activity planning can be done manually by operators, by an activity planning service or a combination.  This message decouples activity planning from allocation, kinematic and other types of planning; the RouteActivityPlan of a System can be created, updated and approved independent of other *Plans.  It enables any type of *Plan to be a constraint on activity planning.
A RouteActivityPlan can be an input and/or output of planning processes.  For example a RouteActivityPlan from a previous round of planning could be an input to an activity planning service that adds additional planned activities to it.

A single System can have multiple independent RouteActivityPlans for different Task, Capability, sensor, etc. types; that are developed by one or more services across a multi-System service oriented architecture; at different times then independently updated and approved.  Optionally, all types of activities for a System can be included in a single RouteActivityPlan.

A RouteActivityPlan can be created discretely or as part of a MissionPlan that includes other *Plans.  A RouteActivityPlan can only be activated and executed as part of a MissionPlan.  A MissionPlan can be used to plan the execution order of multiple RouteActivityPlans and *Plans in general.  A RouteActivityPlan can be subject to approval per Approval* messages.  Planning, approval, activation and execution state information for a RouteActivityPlan are given in other RouteActivityPlan* messages.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1."#]
