#[doc = r#"This message specifies the planned kinematic route of a System.  "Route" is defined as a series of WGS-84 waypoints and is intended for Systems such as aircraft and ground vehicles whose kinematic plans are best represented in an Earth-centered rotational frame.  Route planning can be done manually by operators, by a route planning service or a combination.  This message decouples kinematic planning from allocation, action and other types of planning; the kinematic RoutePlan of a System can be created, updated and approved independent of other *Plans.  It enables any type of *Plan to be a constraint on route planning.

A RoutePlan can be an input and/or output of planning processes.  For example a coarse RoutePlan created by the top System in a hierarchical System of System for overall Mission orchestration and deconfliction could be an input to a route planning service that the produces a detailed, flyable RoutePlan for a specific subordinate System.

A single System can have multiple independent RoutePlans for different types of planned routes such as primary, ingress, egress and contingency.  The different types of routes can be developed by one or more services across a multi-System service oriented architecture at different times then independently updated and approved.  Optionally, all types of routes for a System can be included in a single RoutePlan.

A RoutePlan can be created discretely or as part of a MissionPlan that includes other *Plans.  A RoutePlan can only be activated and executed as part of a MissionPlan.  A MissionPlan can be used to plan the execution order of multiple RoutePlans and *Plans in general.  A RoutePlan can be subject to approval per Approval* messages.  Planning, approval, activation and execution state information for a RoutePlan are given in other RoutePlan* messages.UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1."#]
