#[doc = r#"This message is a Planned C2 request for support from an "external" supporting asset.  The supported asset to supporting asset relationship could be any combination of peer-to-peer, cross-domain, cross-C2-hierarchy, cross-combatant command, joint, coalition, cross-classification, etc.

The taxonomy for UCI Support C2 is the same as the UCI taxonomy for Planned C2, Response C2 and Direct C2.  All four use the same set of "verbs" described in the Effect, Action, Task, Response and [Capability]Command messages.

SupportPlanRequests can include up to five kinds of "actors": requesting system, responding system, supported asset, supporting asset and other constraining asset.  See annotations for associated elements for cardinality and details. 

UCI Support C2 includes planned and direct options.  The UCI Support* messages require a supported asset to have minimal apriori knowledge of the supporting asset and vice-versa as compared to UCI MissionPlan* and related messages.  It can be used in a "broadcast" use case where multiple Systems respond to a single SupportPlanRequest.  The SupportPlanRequestStatus message is "double keyed" to enable the broadcast use case.

This message includes many inputs to the support planning process but many others may come from a variety of other messages.  A few examples of the many inputs include:
1. Options for constraining the planning function in a variety of ways using existing Plans of the same type or by other Plan types.  For example, a SupportPlan could be constrained by a previous SupportPlan.
2. Overrides/refinements of constraints on the Requirements it references.
3. "Weightings" that influence the decisions of operators or planning algorithms performing the planning.
4. Temporal and/or kinematic begin and end points.

See annotations for the SupportPlan message for further details.UCI_PRIMITIVE: ActionRequest-2."#]
